{
  "slug": "compounded",
  "name": "Compounded",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "compounded turns Claude Code skills into a trust-gradient system: every skill earns its autonomy through demonstrated reliability. New skills the agent proposes start as .proposed/, get replayed on a real follow-up task by a verifier subagent (Haiku 4.5) to graduate to .verified/, build a track record to reach .trusted/, and finally graduate to .autonomous/ after 10+ uses with a clean recent run. One correction sends a skill back a tier. Three corrections in 30 days drop it to .proposed.\n\nIncludes cross-project memory (a user-global USER.md auto-injected into every session) and a portable .tar.gz archive for moving your earned skills across machines. v1.1 adds an auto-proposer hook that scores each turn (tool calls, distinct file edits, recovery from failure) and nudges the agent to save high-signal procedures — so you don't have to remember to ask.\n\nNo daemon. No cloud. No telemetry. Python stdlib only. All state in ~/.claude/compounded/ (SQLite + flat files). MIT licensed.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **5 skills**, **1 agent**, **9 commands** and **3 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (5): `compounded-author` (Use this skill when you have just completed a non-trivial task (more than 3 tool calls, novel approach,…), `compounded-trust-tracker` (Use this skill when working with skills already at .verified, .trusted, or .autonomous trust levels — particularly when…), `compounded-typo-fixer` (Use this skill when the user reports a typo in their codebase or documentation and asks for it…), `compounded-verifier` (Use this skill ONLY when invoked as the skill-verifier subagent by compounded's Stop hook), `using-compounded` (Use this skill at the start of any session where compounded is installed, or whenever the user mentions…)\n- **Agents** (1): `skill-verifier` (A subagent dispatched by compounded's Stop hook to decide whether a proposed skill should graduate to .verified or…)\n- **Commands** (9): `demote` (Manually demote a skill one tier (.autonomous → .trusted → .verified → .proposed)), `export` (Export compounded state (USER.md + verified skills) to a portable .tar.gz archive), `import` (Import a compounded archive (.tar.gz produced by `/compounded:export`)), `pin` (Pin a skill at its current trust state, preventing automatic demotion), `status` (Show compounded status — USER.md size, skill counts by trust tier, recent transitions, recent rejections), `trust-status` (Show the compounded trust ladder), `trust` (Manually promote a skill (skip the trust gradient)), `unpin` (Remove a pin from a skill, allowing automatic demotion to resume), and 1 more\n- **Hooks** (3): `SessionStart`, `Stop`, `SessionEnd`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install compounded@claude-community` from `ankitkr3/compounded`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
